{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a novel photoredox-catalyzed oxydifluoromethylation of alkenes using Hu's reagent (N-tosyl-S-difluoromethyl-S-phenylsulfoximine) as a CF2H radical source. Using fac-[Ir(ppy)3] as a photocatalyst under visible light, the method enables the regioselective synthesis of beta-CF2H-substituted alcohols, ethers, and esters from a wide range of terminal and internal alkenes with high functional group tolerance.",
